      "side": 1,
      "message": "In almost all current uses of `for_each_pkvm_guest_vcpu`, except the ones in trace.c, we need struct kvm_vcpu (pkvm_vcpu-\u003evcpu) rather than struct pkvm_vcpu itself, so as a result, we need a bit more boilerplate code to use it. So it seems  it would be better if `for_each_pkvm_guest_vcpu` itself provided struct pkvm_vcpu-\u003evcpu instead (and trace.c would use `to_pkvm_vcpu()` with it)?",
      "revId": "0e2ab888d7855660a8d0ae9e5d97a580cf845694",
