      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can do that. The input will be `struct kvm_vcpu *` and `struct pkvm_vm *`. The macro will be as below:\n```\n  #define for_each_pkvm_guest_vcpu(i, vcpu, vm)                                                   \\\n          for ((i) \u003d 0; (i) \u003c (vm)-\u003ekvm.created_vcpus \u0026\u0026                                          \\\n                        ({ (vcpu) \u003d (vm)-\u003evcpus[(i)] ?                                            \\\n                                    \u0026(vm)-\u003evcpus[(i)]-\u003evcpu : NULL; true; }); (i)++)              \\\n                  if (!(vcpu))                                                                    \\\n                          continue;                                                               \\\n                  else\n```",
